{"nodes": [{"id": "chicken_behavior_analysis_main_chicken_behavior_analysis_main_img_frame025501", "label": "Frame 025501: Infrared View of Flock Dispersed Away From Empty Feed Pans", "file_type": "image", "source_file": "Chicken-Behavior-Analysis-main/Chicken-Behavior-Analysis-main/img/frame025501.png", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": "2022-02-22T08:55:26", "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Monochrome infrared CCTV still, '1080P-IPC-Siren', 2022-02-22 08:55:26, roughly 39 minutes after frame02501 from the same camera and same flock. Birds have re-aggregated into two large drifts on the left and right of the frame, leaving a conspicuous empty aisle of bare litter through the middle beneath the feed line; the pan feeders are empty and almost unattended. The near-identical viewpoint and short time gap make this frame a natural temporal pair with frame02501 for studying flock redistribution between feeding bouts."}, {"id": "chicken_behavior_analysis_main_chicken_behavior_analysis_main_img_frame025501_flock_dispersal_pattern", "label": "Flock Dispersal and Floor Distribution Pattern", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "Chicken-Behavior-Analysis-main/Chicken-Behavior-Analysis-main/img/frame025501.png", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "How birds spread over the litter floor when not feeding \u2014 large drifts against the sides with bare aisles between them. Uneven distribution of this kind is a standard proxy for environmental gradients (temperature, draught, light) inside the house, so the same overhead frames support both behaviour and environment inference."}, {"id": "chicken_behavior_analysis_main_chicken_behavior_analysis_main_img_frame025501_feeder_occupancy_welfare_indicator", "label": "Feeder Occupancy as a Welfare and Health Indicator", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "Chicken-Behavior-Analysis-main/Chicken-Behavior-Analysis-main/img/frame025501.png", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Contrasting frames where pans are full and ringed with birds against frames where pans are empty and unattended shows why the number of birds at the feed line over time is the target signal: a sustained drop relative to the flock's own baseline flags feed-system failure or disease before it is visible in weight records, and it can be measured from imagery alone without touching the birds."}], "edges": [{"source": "chicken_behavior_analysis_main_chicken_behavior_analysis_main_img_frame025501", "target": "chicken_behavior_analysis_main_chicken_behavior_analysis_main_img_frame02101_overhead_cctv_frame", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "Chicken-Behavior-Analysis-main/Chicken-Behavior-Analysis-main/img/frame025501.png", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "chicken_behavior_analysis_main_chicken_behavior_analysis_main_img_frame025501", "target": "chicken_behavior_analysis_main_chicken_behavior_analysis_main_img_frame02101_pan_feeder_line", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "Chicken-Behavior-Analysis-main/Chicken-Behavior-Analysis-main/img/frame025501.png", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "chicken_behavior_analysis_main_chicken_behavior_analysis_main_img_frame025501", "target": "chicken_behavior_analysis_main_chicken_behavior_analysis_main_img_frame025501_flock_dispersal_pattern", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "Chicken-Behavior-Analysis-main/Chicken-Behavior-Analysis-main/img/frame025501.png", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "chicken_behavior_analysis_main_chicken_behavior_analysis_main_img_frame025501", "target": "chicken_behavior_analysis_main_chicken_behavior_analysis_main_img_frame02501", 